## Environments and workflow (read first)

This project runs a strict **local → staging → production** model. The rules below
always apply; the detail lives in the **skills** (`.claude/skills/`), which
**auto-load when your task matches** — listed at the end of this section.

**Branches (two, long-lived).** `{{PROD_BRANCH}}` = production,
`{{STAGING_BRANCH}}` = staging. **Never commit or push directly to either.** All
work is a feature branch cut from `{{STAGING_BRANCH}}`, merged via PR **into
`{{STAGING_BRANCH}}`**. Stacked PRs merge **bottom-up**. Promoting to production is
a deliberate PR from **`{{STAGING_BRANCH}}` → `{{PROD_BRANCH}}`**.

**Environments (three, no shared resources).**

| | git branch | Supabase | {{HOST_PLATFORM}} | API keys |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| **local** | a feature branch | dev branch `{{SUPABASE_DEV_BRANCH_REF}}` | — (`{{DEV_CMD}}`) | local `.env.local` |
| **staging / preview** | `{{STAGING_BRANCH}}` | dev branch `{{SUPABASE_DEV_BRANCH_REF}}` | every Preview deploy | staging keys |
| **production** | `{{PROD_BRANCH}}` | project `{{SUPABASE_PROD_REF}}` | Production deploy | prod keys |

**Nothing but `{{PROD_BRANCH}}` touches a production resource.**

**{{HOST_PLATFORM}} env scoping.** The Production scope holds prod values and
serves `{{PROD_BRANCH}}` only; the Preview scope (all branches) holds staging
values and serves `{{STAGING_BRANCH}}` and every PR preview. Cross-service and
self URLs must be environment-consistent — staging points at staging, prod at
prod, local at localhost. The committed `{{ENV_EXAMPLE_PATH}}` is the **variable
list**; real values live in `.env.local` (local) and the hosting dashboard.

**Database & migrations.** Migrations in `{{MIGRATIONS_DIR}}` **auto-apply to the
dev branch on push to `{{STAGING_BRANCH}}`**; the promotion runs them on prod.
**Never run `supabase db push` or a blanket `supabase migration up` against
production.** Re-seed staging with `{{SEED_SCRIPT_PATH}}`. **Always verify which
database and environment you are writing to before writing.**

**Decision log.** Append **one entry per PR** to the current month's file in
`docs/decisions/` (NOT to CLAUDE.md), then distill any durable conclusion up into
"Current state and standing decisions" below — see the `logging-and-curation`
skill. `.gitattributes` sets `merge=union` on `docs/decisions/*.md` so concurrent
appends auto-resolve — **but only on local merges.** Do integration merges
**locally**, not through the GitHub web UI, or the union driver won't run.

