## Standing Rules (Always Apply)

### Supabase CLI — installed, linked, pointed at the right project

- Any session that touches Supabase must first verify `supabase --version` works
  and `supabase projects list` shows the correct project as **LINKED**.
- **Canonical production project: `{{SUPABASE_PROD_REF}}`.**
- **Persistent staging branch: `{{SUPABASE_DEV_BRANCH_REF}}`.**
{{#ARCHIVE_REF}}
- **`{{SUPABASE_ARCHIVE_REF}}` is a dormant archive — do NOT write to it.**
{{/ARCHIVE_REF}}

### GitHub CLI — installed and authenticated

- Any session doing git work must verify `gh --version` and `gh auth status`.
- Constraints on `gh` usage:
  - **May:** create branches, commit, push, open PRs, comment on issues, view
    PRs/issues.
  - **Must NOT:** merge PRs, close PRs without explicit instruction, force-push,
    delete branches, alter repository settings.
  - **Every PR created by an agent must be reviewed by a human before merge.**

### Decision log — maintained automatically

Every session that makes a **substantive** architectural, schema, or design
decision MUST append an entry to the **current month's file in `docs/decisions/`**
before reporting completion — NOT to CLAUDE.md. Then distill any durable
conclusion up into "Current state and standing decisions" above. "Substantive"
means: schema changes, architecture choices, new dependencies, security-related
changes. Trivial bug fixes don't need an entry. Format:

```markdown
### YYYY-MM-DD — <short title>
**Decision:** what was decided
**Alternatives considered:** what was rejected and why
**Reasoning:** why this choice
**Context:** which prompt or session, link to PR if applicable
```

### Security defaults — never skip

- **RLS enabled on every table by default.** New tables get policies in the same
  commit as table creation.
- **Service role keys are server-side only.** Never browser-exposed, never
  committed to git.
- **All secrets in `.env.local` or platform env vars.** Never inlined in code.
- **Auth validated server-side on every authenticated API route.** Never trust
  client claims.
- **Principle of least privilege:** the `anon` role gets nothing by default.
- **Admin actions write to an append-only audit log.**
- **Soft-delete only; destructive calls are fenced.** Prefer archive/supersede/
  retire over hard deletes; migrations are additive. Any destructive database or
  storage call in app code requires `// destructive-allowed: <reason>` on the
  same or preceding line **plus** human sign-off in PR review (CI: the
  `app-code-scan` job). Never add the annotation to silence the guard.
- **Failures block during development.** Observability and pipeline failures
  THROW and surface; nothing silently continues with unintended behavior. A
  deliberate best-effort path must still log its failure loudly.

### Schema placement — new tables go in the right PostgreSQL schema

| Table kind | Schema |
|---|---|
| Prompt templates / versioned content | `prompts` |
| Audit logs / admin action history | `audit` |
| Operational data | `public` (default) |
| System-managed | `auth`, `storage` — don't touch |

When in doubt, ask before creating a table.

