## 1. Repo layout

<!-- KEEP ONE VARIANT, DELETE THE OTHER. -->

<!-- VARIANT A — monorepo -->
```
{{REPO_NAME}}/
├── apps/                 # deployable applications (own hosting project each)
│   └── {{APP_NAME}}/     # {{APP_DESCRIPTION}} ({{APP_PORT}})
├── packages/             # shared libraries, owned by no single app
│   ├── db/               # the data seam: storage layer + types + SQL schema
│   └── shared/           # client factories, helpers, shared utils
└── docs/                 # specs (authoritative design intent)
```

- **`apps/*`** are deployables; **`packages/*`** are shared libraries.
- Internal packages are named **`{{PACKAGE_SCOPE}}/*`** and depended on via
  **`workspace:*`**.
- **The seam discipline:** the schema, migrations, generated types, and shared
  contracts live **once**, in the package layer, imported by every app. Never
  duplicate the schema; never import one app's internals from another.
- **Dependency direction:** `shared` depends on nothing internal; `db` depends on
  `shared`; `apps/*` depend on packages. **No cycles.** If logic is needed by more
  than one app, promote it into a package rather than importing across an app
  boundary.
- `packages/db` is the only place that talks to the database. Apps call the
  storage layer; they don't hand-roll queries.

