## 2. Tech stack (keep consistent)

{{TECH_STACK}}

- **Read env lazily** — inside request handlers and functions, never at module
  top-level — so builds and imports don't require secrets.

## 3. Data & schema discipline

- **Provenance is mandatory** on derived data: derived rows trace back to their
  sources by id.
- **Raw inputs are append-only.** Derived output is recomputed from the full raw
  corpus, never from prior derived output.
- **History is retained** (trigger-based `*_history` tables) so any prior state is
  reconstructable.
- Migrations live in **`{{MIGRATIONS_DIR}}`**. Generated types live in
  `{{TYPES_PATH}}` — regenerate with `supabase gen types`; don't hand-edit.

## 4. Decision protocol — doneness tags

Specs in `docs/` tag decisions. Respect the tags:

- **[LOCKED]** — a constraint. Implement as written.
- **[OPEN-BLOCKING]** — resolve with a human **before** writing dependent code.
  Ask, don't assume.
- **[OPEN-EXPLORATORY]** — surface 2–4 options to choose from. Do not pick one
  yourself.
- **Untagged** — treat as **[OPEN-BLOCKING]**: ask first.

Do not treat unmarked structure (headers, DDL, prose) as license to expand scope.

## 5. Working discipline

- **Behavior-preserving refactors stay behavior-preserving:** no feature creep, no
  schema changes, no incidental dependency churn.
- **Gate-driven execution:** for multi-step work, stop at the defined boundary and
  report — do not auto-advance.
- **Build in vertical slices**, each testable in isolation; don't jump ahead to
  deferred items.
- **Verify before claiming done:** `{{TYPECHECK_CMD}}`, `{{LINT_CMD}}`,
  `{{BUILD_CMD}}` green on every affected app; state which tier of verification
  you ran, and name the manual click-test a human still needs to run.
- **`docs/` is authoritative** for design intent; update the relevant spec when
  behavior changes.

## 6. Env file convention

```
{{APP_ROOT}}/
├── .env.local       ← actual values, gitignored, never committed
├── .env.example     ← committed template: every var the app reads, placeholder
│                      values, a comment per var (what it does, where to get it)
```

- **Keep `.env.example` in sync**: when an app gains or loses an env var, update
  its `.env.example` in the same commit. No real secrets in examples, ever.
- The root `.gitignore` ignores `.env*` and un-ignores `.env.example`.
- **Deployed apps** get values via the hosting dashboard's Production and Preview
  scopes. Dashboard changes are made by a human with intentional review, not from
  agent sessions.

## 7. Deployment

- Each app deploys as its **own hosting project**, with its Root Directory set to
  the app folder so runtime paths and env vars resolve correctly.
- Apps share one database project; each supplies its own integration env vars.

